---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro'; import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro'; import AudioPlayer from '../../../components/AudioPlayer.astro';
const tracks = [
  { title: 'Midgrave', mp3: '/audio/ann-bonny/mp3/a1-midgrave.mp3', wav: '/audio/ann-bonny/wav/a1-midgrave.wav' },
  { title: 'Poor Random Melody', mp3: '/audio/ann-bonny/mp3/a2-poor-random-melody.mp3', wav: '/audio/ann-bonny/wav/a2-poor-random-melody.wav' },
  { title: 'Jazz-X', mp3: '/audio/ann-bonny/mp3/a3-jazz-x.mp3', wav: '/audio/ann-bonny/wav/a3-jazz-x.wav' },
  { title: 'Match Mort', mp3: '/audio/ann-bonny/mp3/a4-match-mort.mp3', wav: '/audio/ann-bonny/wav/a4-match-mort.wav' },
  { title: 'Notre Dame de tes Morts', mp3: '/audio/ann-bonny/mp3/b1-notre-dame-de-tes-morts.mp3', wav: '/audio/ann-bonny/wav/b1-notre-dame-de-tes-morts.wav' },
  { title: 'Content Warning', mp3: '/audio/ann-bonny/mp3/b2-content-warning.mp3', wav: '/audio/ann-bonny/wav/b2-content-warning.wav' },
  { title: 'Monsters', mp3: '/audio/ann-bonny/mp3/b3-monsters.mp3', wav: '/audio/ann-bonny/wav/b3-monsters.wav' },
  { title: 'I Can Not', mp3: '/audio/ann-bonny/mp3/b4-i-can-not.mp3', wav: '/audio/ann-bonny/wav/b4-i-can-not.wav' },
];
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Ann Bonny — Nee / Söö | Bruit Sourd Press" description="Official press kit for Ann Bonny — Nee / Söö, out October 9, 2026." image="/images/ann-bonny-front.jpg"><Header lang="en" switchPath="/ann-bonny/"/><main>
<section class="relative min-h-screen overflow-hidden"><img src="/images/ann-bonny-front.jpg" alt="Ann Bonny — Nee / Söö" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover" data-parallax/><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black via-black/25 to-black/5"></div><div class="relative mx-auto flex min-h-screen max-w-[1600px] flex-col justify-end px-5 pb-16 pt-36 md:px-8 md:pb-24"><div class="kicker mb-5">Bruit Sourd presents</div><h1 class="display">ANN<br/>BONNY</h1><div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><span class="rounded-full border border-white/40 px-3 py-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[.12em]">Nee / Söö</span><span class="rounded-full border border-white/40 px-3 py-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[.12em]">LP</span><span class="rounded-full border border-white/40 px-3 py-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[.12em]">OCT. 9, 2026</span><span class="rounded-full border border-white/40 px-3 py-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[.12em]">POU045</span><span class="rounded-full border border-white/40 px-3 py-2 text-xs uppercase tracking-[.12em]">EAN 3700398743059</span></div></div></section>
<section class="mx-auto grid max-w-[1600px] gap-12 px-5 py-24 md:px-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_.95fr] lg:py-36"><div class="reveal"><div class="kicker mb-6 text-white/45">Biography</div><h2 class="section-title">A new<br/>story.</h2></div><div class="reveal space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/75"><p><strong class="text-white">Ann Bonny</strong> (1697-?) was a little-known pirate whose life blurred genders, crossed boundaries and rejected convention. Closely associated with John Rackham - and above all Mary Read - she made a mockery of both her fellow pirates and the Royal Navy before disappearing from the historical record after Read's death in 1721, probably at the age of twenty-four.</p><p><strong class="text-white">Ann Bonny</strong> (2020-2022-present) is a shape-shifting trio from eastern France. The appropriate amount of noise. Born from the ashes of 37500 Yens and Rhume Carabiné. Still alive.</p><p>Following directly on from Ma Secte, Ann Bonny grew out of years of intersecting projects and encounters. First came 37500 Yens, then Harpon, then Ma Secte. Eventually everything settled into place: Franck on drums, Jud on bass, and Julie on guitar, vocals and synths.</p><p>After two EPs - the first of which received a cassette release - the trio is bringing both together on vinyl. The record gives full scope to <strong class="text-white">Cherry Jo Lee's</strong> artwork and to the sound shaped by <strong class="text-white">Sylvain Ma at Gnome Studio</strong>, who handled recording, mixing and mastering.</p></div></section>
<section class="mx-auto max-w-[1600px] px-5 pb-24 md:px-8"><img src="/images/ann-bonny-promo.jpeg" alt="Ann Bonny press photo" class="reveal h-auto w-full object-cover grayscale"/></section>
<section class="rule mx-auto max-w-[1600px] px-5 py-24 md:px-8 md:py-36"><div class="max-w-5xl reveal"><div class="kicker mb-6 text-white/45">Blurry-noise</div><p class="section-title">Violence.<br/>Darkness.<br/>Breath cut short.</p><p class="mt-10 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-white/65">The band calls it blurry-noise. More concretely: the pressure and abrasion of Chat Pile, melodies brushing against YC-CY, uncertain rhythms and an appetite for everything unstable, awkward and unsettling in contemporary chamber music. Through the weight of it all, Julie's voice remains soft, fragile and almost suspended.</p></div></section>
<section class="mx-auto grid max-w-[1600px] gap-10 px-5 py-24 md:px-8 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:py-36"><img src="/images/ann-bonny-back.jpg" alt="Ann Bonny back cover artwork" class="reveal w-full"/><div class="reveal self-end"><div class="kicker mb-6 text-white/45">Artwork</div><h2 class="section-title">Cherry<br/>Jo Lee.</h2><p class="mt-8 max-w-xl text-lg text-white/65">The record's illustrations extend its darkness, humour and taste for hybrid forms.</p></div></section>
<AudioPlayer tracks={tracks} lang="en"/>
<section class="rule mx-auto max-w-[1600px] px-5 py-24 md:px-8 md:py-36"><div class="max-w-5xl"><div class="kicker mb-6 text-white/45">October 9, 2026</div><p class="section-title">This is not the return of 37500 Yens.<br/>It is a new story.</p><a href="/en/37500-yens/" class="btn mt-10">Discover Astero →</a></div></section>
</main><Footer lang="en"/></BaseLayout>